{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":55611,"ns":0,"title":"Alexandroff extension","extract":"In the mathematical field of topology, the Alexandroff extension is a way to extend a noncompact topological space by adjoining a single point in such a way that the resulting space is compact.  It is named after the Russian mathematician Pavel Alexandroff.","description":"Way to extend a non-compact topological space","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}